TypeScript Lesson 16: public, private, protected & abstract 🔐
Aaj hum seekhenge ki class ke data ko control kaise karte hain aur abstract class ka use karke common structure kaise banate hain.
1. public — sab jagah access
public property ko class ke bahar se bhi access kar sakte hain. TypeScript mein class members default se public hote hain.
class Employee {
    public name: string;

    constructor(name: string) {
        this.name = name;
    }
}

const emp = new Employee("Rahul");

console.log(emp.name); // Rahul
emp.name = "Amit";     // Allowed
console.log(emp.name); // Amit


2. private — sirf class ke andar
Maan lo bank account ka balance har jagah directly change nahi hona chahiye.
class BankAccount {
    private balance: number = 1000;

    showBalance(): void {
        console.log(this.balance);
    }
}

const account = new BankAccount();

account.showBalance(); // 1000

// account.balance = 5000; // TypeScript error


balance ko class ke bahar directly access nahi kar sakte, lekin class ka apna method use kar sakta hai.
3. protected — parent aur child class
protected member ko us class ke andar aur uski child classes mein access kar sakte hain, lekin class ke bahar directly nahi.
class Animal {
    protected name: string;

    constructor(name: string) {
        this.name = name;
    }
}

class Dog extends Animal {
    showName(): void {
        console.log(this.name);
    }
}

const dog = new Dog("Tommy");

dog.showName(); // Tommy

// console.log(dog.name); // TypeScript error


Yaad rakhne ka shortcut:
Modifier	Class ke andar	Child class	Bahar se
public	Yes	Yes	Yes
protected	Yes	Yes	No
private	Yes	No, directly nahi	No
Ye TypeScript ke private aur protected access rules hain.
4. abstract class kya hoti hai?
Abstract class ek base design hoti hai. Isse directly object nahi bana sakte; doosri class ise extend karke implement karti hai.
Maan lo har shape ka area hota hai, lekin circle aur rectangle ka area calculate karne ka formula alag hai.
abstract class Shape {
    abstract area(): number;

    showArea(): void {
        console.log("Area:", this.area());
    }
}

class Rectangle extends Shape {
    constructor(
        private length: number,
        private width: number
    ) {
        super();
    }

    override area(): number {
        return this.length * this.width;
    }
}

const rectangle = new Rectangle(10, 5);

rectangle.showArea(); // Area: 50


Samjho:
- abstract class Shape — base class, iska direct object nahi bana sakte.
- abstract area(): number — child class ko area() implement karna hoga.
- extends Shape — Rectangle, Shape ko inherit karta hai.
- super() — parent constructor call karta hai.
- override area() — Rectangle apna area formula define karta hai.
Agar Rectangle ne area() implement nahi kiya, to TypeScript error dega.

